INTRODUCTION 
Population and Housing Censuses in Fiji are conducted every ten years. Having major 
exercises of this nature conducted every ten years presents a major challenge for Census 
takers in terms of knowledge and experience retention. The Administrative Report serves 
as a detailed documentation of the experiences from this massive administrative and 
logistical exercise. 
The administrative report therefore covers the activities and standards that were put in 
place to guide the conduct of the 2017 Population and Housing Census, in particular, 
the different levels of engagement with government agencies and key stakeholders who 
played important roles in the whole exercise. The details are provided in the sections 
that follow. 
To set a clear direction for all individuals who were part of the national project, a vision 
was created through wide consultations with our Divisional Offices including Area 
Coordinators. The notion of involving the Area Coordinators was to provide management 
a framework of slowly delegating ownership of all preparatory activities towards the 
lower levels of the Census Organization hierarchy on what was expected of the National 
exercise. 
The vision was then set for “an inclusive 2017 Population and Housing Census coverage 
for the provision of high quality data ”.  The mission was “a n Innovative and Efficient 
National Survey Operation achieved through Great Team work ”. It was the 
management’s responsibility to create the most effective strategies possible to 
accomplish both. The vision and mission also helped guide evaluations and 
improvements throughout the entire Census process. It created a firm foundation of a 
successful Census. 
The subsections in this document entails a summary of logistics.  It includes the 
methodological preparation, innovations, training and collection.  It captures the 
various activities with scheduled dates and challenges so as to give a full portrait of 
what had transpired in the 2017 Census on the following.   
1. Mapping
2. Budget
3. Human resource
4. Questionnaire design
5. Publicity
