information.  The Government Statistician/Census Commisioner Secretary was also 
given a minute track sheet to track all submissions coming in.  It was a way of 
monitoring that all submissions came as scheduled as per the individual work plan for 
the respective nine teams. 
 
There were Divisional visits by the Census Commissioner and Census Director. 
Monitoring by respective team leaders were, however, planned well in advance and 
requested formally.  Divisional managers were advised on the same to ensure minimal 
disturbance to the work being undertaken.  
 
 
