South to South Cooperation 
 
Preparatory work for the 2017 Census also involved FBoS staff observing operations 
during the Vanuatu Mini Census and Tongan National Census.  The study visit 
facilitated a lot of information sharing on the requirements of a digital census and this 
gave us greater clarity on a number of issues. Valuable lessons were gained in the 
manner in which challenges associated with the adoption of new technology were dealt 
with during the early stages of enumeration. 
 
Risk Assessment and Mitigation Strategy 
 
A Risk Assessment and Mitigation Strategy was developed as this was Fiji’s first Digital 
Census. A Census Processes and Programme Standard was put in place after four 
scheduled 2017 Census meetings and the operational plan developed included a Risk 
Assessment.  Mitigation strategies were also put in place to ensure the Census goals 
and objectives were achieved. 
 
The following steps were considered for the risk assessment and mitigation process; 

2017 Population and Housing Census, Administrative Report, 2018 
Page 17 
 
 
1. Identification of risks 
 
Respective subcommittees were advised to identify specific risks related to activities for 
their teams through consultation with committee members.  They were instructed to 
define each risk in a concise manner.  To help with the process, the WWF template was 
used. 
The WWF process looks at a range of risk categories:  Political, Economic, Social, 
Technical, Capacity, Financial, Infrastructure, Partner, Leadership, and Management.  
The teams used the categories that were relevant i.e. where potential risks were 
identified.  
 
2. Ranking of risks 
 
The risks were also ranked to the probability of occurrence as outlined below; 
i. communication breakdown  
ii. transport logistics 
iii. clear enumeration area boundary ID 
iv. IT resources management 
v. undercount of EAs 
vi. financial resources  
vii. HQ data monitoring 
viii. consistency for the overall management of the project 
ix. request for external consultants for data processing 
  
