The Department was allocated a total sum of FJD22m for the 2017 Census, an 
indication of the Fijian Government’s support for the Census. The Department put 
together small area level budgets (Enumeration Area level) which required a fair bit of 
work. The accompanying justifications were equally detailed ensuring the availability of 
relevant information when required for the assessment phase. The Department 
approach of preparing Small area level budgets does require a very good level of local 
area knowledge. Pre-planned activities proceeded concurrently. 
 
For the period August 2016 to July 2017, a sum of FJD 7.9m was allocated. A sum of 
$14.5m was committed by the Fiji government for the financial year August 2017 to 
July 2018. This required submissions to release the funds on a quarterly basis.   
 
The utilization of Census funds was closely monitored with regular feedback provided 
to the subcommittees during the scheduled meetings. A budget review was conducted 
in each quarter to review the various allocations and their utilization. Where marginal 
and necessary priorities were needed, the Census Commissioners’ cautious decisions 
on the use of contingency funds provided sufficient flexibility and this ensured that the 
planned activities proceeded as planned. 
 
Standard Operating Procedures 
 
Table 3: Standard Operating Procedures 
Accountable Advance  
a) Accountable Advance should be cleared/ retired at the conclusion of each lot date 
of project visit.  
b) New accountable advance will only be issued once previous issued accountable 
advance has been cleared/ retired at level 5 Accounts section. 
c) Only those that  have completely retired/ cleared accountable advance, will 
proceed to the next phase of fieldwork. 
d) Officers will be allocated appropriate amount of accountable advance for each 
lot, not for entire rounds. 
e) Additional accountable advance for unforeseen circ umstances to be requested 
through normal request.  
2017 Population and Housing Census, Administrative Report, 2018 
Page 20 
 
Retirement of claims 
a) The retirements of claims should be made within 7 days to a maximum of 14 
working days upon return to the station/ office. 
b) The request for the next accountable advance shall only be made upon clearance 
of the previous claims. 
c) All receipts of expenses incurred during the course of fieldwork shall be attached 
with a completed and signed claim form by the officer. 
d) All transactions to be issued with official receipts from service providers 
e) All receipts for travelling in a vehicle should contain the following information; 
− drivers full name, phone number, vehicle registration number, driver’s 
signature, duration of use of vehicle and the localities visited and purpose. 
f) All claim forms shall be checked and signed by the field statistician. 
g) The use of imprest receipts will be considered on a case by case basis. 
 
Contingencies 
a) Contingency fund will be controlled by accounts. 
b) Request for extra fund should be made through a formal request. 
 
Transport 
a) The use of private and own vehicles will not be entertained for any fieldwork. 
b) Government vehicles will be used only for officers who are not given any transport 
allowance. 
c) All office must keep and update a transport register. 
d) All drivers are to fill in their running sheet daily and submit weekly to the 
transport officer. 
e) In areas where public transport is available and easily accessible, officers shall 
use public transport eg. Taxis and buses. 
f) In areas where public transport is not readily availa ble, officers shall use other 
means of transportation in order to complete the assigned duties in the required 
time frame.  Official receipts must be obtained. 
g) Usage of taxis for hire for field operation shall be encouraged in town and city 
areas. 
h) In roads  and localities where taxis do not want to provide services due to 
accessibility and road conditions, especially in the peri - urban and rural areas, 
officers may use other means of transportation to complete the task on time. 
i) Availability of taxis after hours is a concern in Western and Northern division. As 
such officers shall use any other means of transportation available at those times.  
Official receipts must be obtained. 
 
  
