The revision of Enumeration Area boundaries was a critical part of the Census 
preparation. The whole objective was to ensure an even workload for the Enumerators 
during data collection. Thus, the mapping exercise aimed to produce clearly demarcated 
boundaries on High quality maps. 
SPC provided Technical Assistance during the early stages of work. Detailed planning 
with strict set targets for the mapping work helped in the production of high quality EA 
Maps. 
It was the responsibility of the Mapping committee to update all Enumeration Area (EA) 
Maps before the recruitment of Supervisors and Enumerators.  All EA maps contained 
detailed and up-to date information that was helpful in guiding the data collectors in 
their assigned EA. 
The Mapping team was also tasked with the plotting of GPS waypoints of the informal 
settlements, as illustrated below.  This was used as a monitoring tool during Census 
enumeration. 
  
