INNOVATIVE APPROACHES 
 
A partnership was developed with Drones Fiji Limited to improve the aerial imagery of 
informal settlements along the Lami-Suva-Nasinu-Nausori corridor which are densely 
populated and presents major challenges for data collection. The use of drone imagery 
eased the identification of EA boundaries which were overlaid on very clear images of 
an area’s physical and natural features such as roads, creeks, building structures and 
vegetation. This contributed to good coverage during the Census. 
 
Figure 9: TopoDrone 4Scight 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
The TopoDrone 4Scight was used for precision mapping which required no ground 
control points. 
Five drone pilots were tasked by Drone Services Fiji to capture and map the 27 squatter 
regions.  In a span of a week, FBoS was able to map out 27 squatter settlements with 
accurate and updated information.  This was uploaded to Google map which was  
accessible by field officers, in particular the area coordinators.   Links to the media 
coverage are attached in appendix 13. 
 
  

