The Recruitment process for Census staff required meticulous planning with great 
attention to detail. Trial runs were carried out to ensure that all applicants were 
efficiently taken through the various test exercises. 
 
The Staffing Establishment for the 2017 Population and Housing Census was 
approved by the Minister for Economy. The advertisement for the first 172 positions 
was approved by the Civil Service Reform Management Unit. The following positions 
were advertised on Saturday 24 December 2016 which ran for 3 weeks and closed on 
16/01/2017. 
 
 Area Coordinators - 150 
 Statistical Officer - 05 
 Analyst - 01 
 Assistant Analyst - 01 
 Asst. Accts Officer - 01 
 Accts Clerk - 05 
 Data Verifier’s - 03 
 Admin Clerk - 01 
 Drivers - 05 
 
The recruitment process for Area Coordinators (150) started in January 2017 and was 
followed by the recruitment of Supervisors (650) and then the recruitment of 
Enumerators (2156).  The aim for the initial recruitment of the 150 Area Coordinators 
around November 2016 was to have them start work in January 2017.  The early 
engagement of the Area Coordinators allowed their involvement in most of the 
preparatory activities including their role as Enumerators for the Pilot Test in April 
2017. Their roles and responsibilities was planned and clearly defined in the months 
2017 Population and Housing Census, Administrative Report, 2018 
Page 34 
 
leading up to the Census, particularly the period prior to the recruitment of Supervisors 
and Enumerators. 
 
RECRUITMENT OF 650 SUPERVIOSRS & 2156 ENUMERATORS 
 
The HR team conducted their recruitment drive for Supervisors and Enumerators from 
Thursday 1st June to Wednesday 28th June 2017. The public were informed of the 
Recruitment Centres through advertisements in the dailies and all interested individuals 
were requested to apply in person only once. Applicants were advised on the 
entitlements of those selected to be part of the Census exercise. 
Requirements    
Those to be recruited were to be Fiji Citizen, physically fit and under the age of 55 years.  
It is the responsibility of the interested applicant to bring in copies of; 
− Birth Certificate  
− Tin Letter  
− FNPF  
 
Knowledge of smart devices will be an added advantage. 
 
Grievance procedure 
 
For the entire operation, all grievances followed the proper channel as per the line of 
reporting in Figure 2 and was addressed only by the HR committee where necessary.  It 
included; 
 
1. Causalities whilst in the field 
2. Disagreements between officers on certain areas of work 
3. Complaints against officers not performing to expectations 
4. Harassment of any form 
5. Concerns on allowances and pay 
6. Concerns from the general public 
7. Any other grievance for that matter 
 
