Capacity Strengthening of FBoS in gender mainstreaming and gender statistics 
compilation was an important aspect in the formulation of 2017 Census questionnaire 
and this reflected a commitment to the new phase of the Project “Progressing Gender 
Equality in the Pacific Island Countries” (PGEP 2). 
 
The first Questionnaire test for the flow of questions and its structure was conducted 
on the 29th of September, 2016 with the survey solutions tester uploaded on 20 tablets. 
Team Leaders of the nine subcommittees and all concerned officers participated. The 
length of the form was also tested to indicate the length of time to enumerate a 
household as such the enumerator workload.  Additionally, the testing also revealed 
how well the questions were understood and whether there were any difficulties in 
answering them.   
 
The numerous requests from stakeholders were considered as FBoS tried to meet the 
needs of a wide range of users. Stakeholders were advised that the Census is not 
suitable for the collection of detailed information. The availability of alternative sources 
of information was also considered.  
 
Prior to the user group consultation, two workshops involving government stakeholders 
were conducted and this was to allow early engagement and this was maintained 
throughout the Census operation.  The following list of activities illustrates the wide 
range of consultation undertaken to shape the Census Questionnaire. 
 
