2. International Labour Organisation (ILO) (CL & ICLS concept) 
 
Child labour training 
 
 A Child labour data collection and analysis training was conducted for the 
ACs from the 9th to the 11th of May. The overall aim was to promote the 
collection of national data on child labour and education through the census, 
socio economic surveys, labour force surveys and other national surveys.  
 
The training helped the Area Coordinators; 
i. Understand child labour concepts and legal frameworks to promote quality 
data collection in the 2017 Fiji census 
ii. Assess the links between Census questions and child labour data analysis 
iii. Prepare for training of 2017 Census Enumerators 
 
ICLS concept 
 
The ILO’s Regional Statistician, ROAP Bangkok Mission to Fiji on 02 - 05 May 2017 - 
CPO FJI127 was beneficial to us following his presentation to the AC’s on the ICLS 
concept of Economic Activity with special reference to Module D on Economic Activities 
Last Week. The contents of the presentation also helped in building FBoS’ capacity to 
produce regular reports on the SDGs decent work indicators. 
 
3. SPC (Questionnaire design, Mapping & Gender Perspectives) 
 
Questionnaire design  
 
The Fiji Bureau of Statistics sought the assistance of the Pacific Community’s 
Statistics for Development Division (SDD) to provide CAPI training for the 
proposed ILO/SPC Census questions. The technical support and plans were developed 
within the framework of Phase 2 (2015-2017) of the Ten Year Pacific Statistics 
Development Strategy (TYPSS). Cost sharing arrangements was made with regards to 
the TA and SDD also helped in the justification and procurement of tablets. 
 
