The Department was allocated a total sum of FJD22m for the 2017 Census, an
indication of the Fijian Government’s support for the Census. The Department put
together small area level budgets (Enumeration Area level) which required a fair bit of
work. The accompanying justifications were equally detailed ensuring the availability of
relevant information when required for the assessment phase. The Department
approach of preparing Small area level budgets does require a very good level of local
area knowledge. Pre-planned activities proceeded concurrently.
For the period August 2016 to July 2017, a sum of FJD 7.9m was allocated. A sum of
$14.5m was committed by the Fiji government for the financial year August 2017 to
July 2018. This required submissions to release the funds on a quarterly basis.
The utilization of Census funds was closely monitored with regular feedback provided
to the subcommittees during the scheduled meetings. A budget review was conducted
in each quarter to review the various allocations and their utilization. Where margi

